    <title>Physical Exam</title>
    <text><paragraph>Vital signs recorded on 1996-03-10; see the Vital Signs section. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>General</td><td>Alert, humorous, and engaged; reduced facial expression</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiovascular</td><td>Regular rhythm at 70 per minute. Blood pressure 128/80 mmHg after 5 minutes supine and 122/78 mmHg after 3 minutes standing, without symptoms; no orthostatic hypotension</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>In the on state about two hours after a dose: MDS-UPDRS Part III 30, Hoehn and Yahr stage 2.5. Bilateral bradykinesia and rigidity, worse on the right; mild right-hand rest tremor; soft, monotone speech; no dyskinesia</td></tr><tr><td>Gait</td><td>Short steps with reduced arm swing; recovers unaided after three steps on the pull test; Timed Up and Go 13 seconds</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

