  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Parkinson&apos;s disease, Hoehn and Yahr stage 2.5 (G20.A1)</content>. Neurology confirms clinically established Parkinson&apos;s disease by the MDS criteria. Bradykinesia limits daily tasks on a modest levodopa dose, with no motor fluctuations or dyskinesia. No orthostatic hypotension. No falls, but short steps and a slowed pull-test recovery mean his fall risk is rising. [S]<list><item>Increase carbidopa-levodopa to one and a half 25/100 mg tablets (levodopa 150 mg) three times daily, 30 minutes before meals, as neurology advises.</item><item>Spread protein through the day rather than taking doses with a large protein meal.</item><item>Physical therapy for gait, balance, and a home exercise program of at least 150 minutes a week.</item><item>Supine and standing blood pressure at the three-month review, after the dose increase.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hypokinetic dysarthria with soft speech (R47.1)</content>. Soft, monotone speech, with intelligibility reduced in noise. [S]<list><item>Four-week intensive speech therapy course (LSVT LOUD), starting next week.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>MDS-UPDRS Parts III and IV and Hoehn and Yahr stage</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Part III 30 in the on state; Hoehn and Yahr 2.5; Part IV: no dyskinesia, wearing-off, or on-off</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Orthostatic blood pressure, supine and after 3 minutes standing</td><td>Every visit while on dopaminergic treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>128/80 mmHg supine and 122/78 mmHg at 3 minutes standing; no orthostatic hypotension</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Dopaminergic regimen review for wearing-off, dyskinesia, and on-off</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No motor complications; bradykinesia limits daily tasks, so levodopa is increased to 150 mg three times daily before meals</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Avoidance of dopamine-blocking drugs</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No antipsychotic, metoclopramide, or prochlorperazine; ondansetron is the antiemetic of choice if one is ever needed</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Medication side effects and adherence</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No nausea or sleepiness; no missed doses, though doses are often taken with meals</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fall query and fall-risk assessment (Timed Up and Go, pull test)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls or near falls; Timed Up and Go 13 seconds; recovers after three steps on the pull test</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Psychotic symptoms (hallucinations, delusions)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Impulse-control screen (QUIP-RS)</td><td>Every visit; mandatory on a dopamine agonist</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Negative; not on a dopamine agonist</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Exercise counseling: aerobic, resistance, and balance, at least 150 minutes a week</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Walks 30 minutes most days; physical therapy will add balance and strength work toward 150 minutes a week</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Advance care planning and goals of care</td><td>At diagnosis and at least yearly</td><td>Due</td><td>Planned for the preventive visit in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Diagnosis review against the MDS clinical diagnostic criteria</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Movement disorders neurology confirms clinically established Parkinson&apos;s disease: bradykinesia with rest tremor and rigidity, a clear response to levodopa, and no red flags</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Cognitive screen (MoCA)</td><td>At least yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>MoCA 27 of 30 four weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression, anxiety, and apathy (PHQ-9)</td><td>At least yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PHQ-9 3 four weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Sleep: REM sleep behavior disorder questionnaire, Epworth Sleepiness Scale, insomnia, restless legs</td><td>At least yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Negative REM sleep behavior disorder screen and Epworth score 6 four weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Autonomic symptoms: constipation, urinary, sexual, sweating, drooling</td><td>At least yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No autonomic symptoms four weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Swallowing screen (EAT-10)</td><td>At least yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>EAT-10 score 2 four weeks ago, below the threshold of 3</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Speech and voice loudness</td><td>Yearly; speech therapy for speech change</td><td>Referred</td><td>Soft, monotone speech; four-week LSVT LOUD course starts next week</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Physical, occupational, and speech therapy</td><td>At diagnosis, then reassessed yearly</td><td>Referred</td><td>Physical therapy for gait and balance and speech therapy arranged; occupational therapy not needed now because he is independent in daily activities</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Movement disorders neurology consultation</td><td>At diagnosis, then yearly or with a change</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seen today for diagnosis review, levodopa adjustment, and rehabilitation planning</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Genetic testing with counseling</td><td>Once, offered to every person with Parkinson&apos;s disease</td><td>Due</td><td>Offered by neurology today with counseling; he will decide at the yearly neurology review</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Dental and oral examination</td><td>Every 6 months</td><td>Due</td><td>No dental visit on record; to be arranged</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Driving safety</td><td>Yearly or with a motor or cognitive change</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Drives short local trips in daylight; MoCA 27 and no daytime sleepiness four weeks ago; review yearly or with any change</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Vaccination status (influenza, pneumococcal, zoster, COVID-19, Tdap)</td><td>Yearly, per the CDC schedule</td><td>Due</td><td>Influenza vaccine given last autumn; pneumococcal, zoster, COVID-19, and Tdap to be reviewed at the preventive visit</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Routine laboratory monitoring</td><td>Not required for Parkinson&apos;s disease surveillance</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>The CMID monograph calls for no routine laboratory tests; baseline blood count, chemistry, vitamin B12, and TSH were normal at the first visit</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Brain MRI</td><td>If atypical parkinsonism features appear</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No atypical features; neurology agrees no imaging is needed</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Polysomnography for REM sleep behavior disorder</td><td>If REM sleep behavior disorder treatment is considered</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No dream enactment</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>AGS Beers Criteria medication review</td><td>Yearly from age 65</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>He is 54</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Deep brain stimulation programming review</td><td>Every 6 to 12 months after implantation</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No deep brain stimulator</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Less slowness of movement after a levodopa adjustment, without dyskinesia or orthostatic hypotension, by the three-month review. In progress; target 1996-06-09 [S]</item><item>Complete a four-week intensive speech therapy course and keep up daily voice practice. In progress; target 1996-06-09 [S]</item><item>No falls through the six-month review, with at least 150 minutes a week of exercise including balance work. In progress; target 1996-09-08 [S]</item><item>Name a health care agent and record his goals of care by the preventive visit. In progress; target 1996-10-06 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Dopaminergic Therapy for Motor Symptoms in Early Parkinson Disease Practice Guideline Summary: A Report of the AAN Guideline Subcommittee (2021); MDS clinical diagnostic criteria for Parkinson&apos;s disease (2015); The recommendations of a consensus panel for the screening, diagnosis, and treatment of neurogenic orthostatic hypotension and associated supine hypertension (2017); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Parkinson&apos;s disease monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Three-month Parkinson&apos;s disease review, with supine and standing blood pressure after the levodopa increase. Speech therapy starts next week and physical therapy within two weeks. Next scheduled visit 1996-06-09: three-month Parkinson&apos;s disease review after the levodopa increase and speech therapy. [S]</paragraph></text>

